# Cloudflare Pages — trailing slash loop prevention
#
# CF Pages' static asset server issues a 301 to add a trailing slash when
# a directory exists (e.g. /Account/SignIn → /Account/SignIn/). The CF
# Pages Function then strips it back (301 to /Account/SignIn), creating
# an infinite redirect loop.
#
# 200 rewrites intercept BEFORE CF's trailing slash logic fires and serve
# the directory index directly — no redirect issued, URL stays clean.
#
# Note: CF Pages _redirects matching is case-insensitive, but the
# [[Path]].ts edge function runs first and redirects lowercase variants
# to the PascalCase canonical before _redirects is consulted.

/Account/ForgotPassword /Account/ForgotPassword/ 200
/Account/ResetPassword /Account/ResetPassword/ 200
/Account/SignIn /Account/SignIn/ 200
/Account/SignUp /Account/SignUp/ 200
/Blog /Blog/ 200
/Contact/Sale /Contact/Sale/ 200
/Contributing /Contributing/ 200
/Dashboard /Dashboard/ 200
/Doc /Doc/ 200
/Download /Download/ 200
/Legal/Privacy /Legal/Privacy/ 200
/Legal/Term /Legal/Term/ 200
/License /License/ 200
/OAuth/Success /OAuth/Success/ 200
/Portal /Portal/ 200
/Verify /Verify/ 200
